INT. DECOMMISSIONED LIGHTHOUSE - LAMP ROOM - DAY

Salt-fogged glass wraps the room in a cold white glare. Six folding chairs have been arranged in a circle around the great Fresnel lens, as though the lens itself were the facilitator. A flip chart reads, in bubbly marker: "SYNERGY IS A VERB."

PRISCILLA OKONKWO-HALE (50s, silk scarf, lanyard worn like a medal) stands beside the flip chart with a laser pointer. GREGOR "GIGGLES" LINDQVIST (40s, never once seen laughing) slumps in the nearest chair. MARISOL TREJO (30s, spreadsheet-pale) clutches a gluten-free muffin. BARNABY FIELD (60s, tie knotted for a funeral) reads the safety placard on the wall. DEEPA RAMANATHAN (30s, sharp, phone face-down on her knee) watches the door. HOLLIS PYM (20s, intern, sunburned already) hugs a box of markers.

PRISCILLA
Okay, team. Check-in. One word for how you're showing up today. Gregor, let's start with you.

GIGGLES
Present.

PRISCILLA
That's not a feeling, Giggles.

GIGGLES
It's the only one I'm contractually obliged to have.

MARISOL
Priscilla, the ferry doesn't come back until six. Is that right? Because the booking said "overnight optional."

PRISCILLA
Marisol, the beauty of an island is that we're all optional together.

BARNABY
Priscilla, with respect, the placard says the gallery railing is rated for four persons. We are six, plus the lens.

DEEPA
Barnaby, the lens doesn't count as a person.

BARNABY
Deepa, it has more seniority than Hollis.

HOLLIS
That's fair, Barnaby. Honestly, that's fair.

PRISCILLA
Hollis, sweetheart, I need you to stay in your lane and also grow.

HOLLIS
Which lane is that, Priscilla?

PRISCILLA
The one with the markers.

DEEPA
Giggles, did you read the pre-work? Because I read the pre-work, and the pre-work said we'd be "dismantling silos," and I don't see a single silo, I see a lighthouse.

GIGGLES
Deepa, a lighthouse is just a silo with ambitions.

MARISOL
Giggles, that's the nicest thing you've said all quarter.

GIGGLES
Marisol, it wasn't nice. It was accurate.

PRISCILLA
Everyone, eyes up. Barnaby, put the placard down. Deepa, phone. Marisol, muffin. Hollis, marker. Giggles, whatever that is, stop.

BARNABY
Priscilla, I would like it noted that I have been with this company for thirty-one years and have never once been asked to hold a marker.

PRISCILLA
Noted, Barnaby. Noted and parked.

DEEPA
Parked where? There's no parking. It's an island.
